CHAPTER 2
Notice and Opportunity to Be Heard
Procedure has the distinction of claiming the only right to be mentioned twice in the United States Constitution: due process.

U.S. Constitution, Amendment V
No person * * * shall * * * be deprived of life, liberty, or property, without due process of law * * * .

U.S. Constitution, Amendment XIV, Section 1
* * * No State shall * * * deprive any person of life, liberty, or property, without due process of law; * * * .



•An action violates due process when

1.The State (or the United States)

2.deprives a person of life, liberty, or property

3.without “due process of law”
